It shouldn't close the connection automatically on that; it should toss
the save out and let you continue.  I'll look and see what's up there.

> Seems to be the only way to stop a wizard from winning.

The changes I'm making aren't about "stopping" anyone, though certain
fringe elements seem compelled to believe they are.

The intent is to add more variety and replayability into the game, even
(possibly 'especially') for those who are highly skilled at the game.

In some cases... such as Elbereth... what that will mean is removing the
no-brainer solution to a problem, such that players are encouraged to
use the natural ingenuity they already possess as well as other
resources currently available within the game, or newly added resources.

I feel confident that Nethack players are quite capable of solving such
problems, even though no explicit solution has been laid out.

